# Runs through /usr/local/bin/omni-manage (infra/host/omni-manage.sh), which waits out a
# blue/green deploy window instead of failing with "backend is not running" (2026-09-04).
# Time Doctor workforce pull — THREE settle pulls a day (CFO 2026-08-01).
#
# Some machines upload their hours to Time Doctor LATE (in delayed batches when
# they sync). A single early pull then judges a day before its data arrived and
# wrongly reports "did not track". So we pull the SAME day three times and let
# hris.people_data_guard tell a settled figure from one still arriving:
#
#   03:00 SAST (01:00 UTC)  slot 0300  — first look (most PCs still off)
#   04:00 SAST (02:00 UTC)  slot 0400  — second look
#   04:30 SAST (02:30 UTC)  slot 0430  — extra look feeding the 07:05 accuracy check
#   08:30 SAST (06:30 UTC)  slot 0830  — final backstop look, AFTER people boot up
#   15:50 SAST (13:50 UTC)  slot 1550  — LATE CATCH-UP for back-filled hours
#
# CFO 2026-09-09, checklist L28. The 0830 pull was the LAST look at a day, and
# Time Doctor keeps ADDING to a past day as offline machines upload what they
# buffered. So the stored snapshot froze at a figure everyone downstream then
# read as final. One employee's power cut left her snapshot at 1.74 h while Time
# Doctor held 3.24 h, and she reported it twice. The permanent record and the
# leave-docking path now read live (integrations.td_live) and never revise
# downward — but the readers that CANNOT afford a live call still read this
# snapshot: reporting/cost_per_hour (a whole month, inside a web request, no
# cache — live pulls there would time the page out), the Telegram view, the
# reconciliation view and the healthcheck. This 15:50 pull refreshes the day for
# all of them, and lands BEFORE the 16:10 SAST record reconcile and the 16:25
# deduction enforcement so both see the better figure too.
#
# CFO 2026-08-05: the consolidated 07:05 Morning Brief runs its DeepSeek/Gemini
# people-data accuracy check at send time over ALL settle samples, so the new
# 04:30 pull gives that check more-settled data and makes the 07:05 report
# trustworthy that early. When CONSOLIDATED_EMAILS_ENABLED is ON the 0830 pull
# no longer emails a standalone report (folded into the 07:05 brief); it stays a
# backstop settle pull.
#
# Each pull records a per-user tracked-seconds sample under its slot WITHOUT
# wiping the earlier slots (get_or_create). Skips gracefully if no TIMEDOCTOR_TOKEN
# (env or CFO Vault) is set. Drop into /etc/cron.d/ (sudo cp + chmod 644). Clock is UTC.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
0 1 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage pull_timedoctor --slot 0300 --no-email >> /var/log/timedoctor-pull.log 2>&1
0 2 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage pull_timedoctor --slot 0400 --no-email >> /var/log/timedoctor-pull.log 2>&1
30 2 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage pull_timedoctor --slot 0430 --no-email >> /var/log/timedoctor-pull.log 2>&1
30 6 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage pull_timedoctor --slot 0830 >> /var/log/timedoctor-pull.log 2>&1
50 13 * * * root cd /opt/alpha-finance && /usr/local/bin/omni-manage pull_timedoctor --slot 1550 --no-email >> /var/log/timedoctor-pull.log 2>&1
